  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is for multimodal multiprofile models with avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion, with config_019 achieving the best validation accuracy (0.639) and F1 (0.620). The major untested design choice in this promising region is RNA representation, since only PCA has been evaluated. config_031 keeps the current best profile setting, image encoder, aggregation, and fusion fixed while replacing PCA with scvi_n200, directly testing whether a learned RNA encoder improves the current best multimodal setup. This is a one-factor extension of the most promising direction, balancing exploitation of the current best configuration with exploration of an important untested representation choice, and it can either produce a new best result or efficiently rule out scvi before spending more experiments on related variants."
}

